  "descriptionRussian": "Страдательный залог с -ся и причастиями",
  "imageName": "arrow.uturn.left",
  "intro": "Russian has two main ways to form passive voice. 1) REFLEXIVE PASSIVE with -СЯ (imperfective, ongoing/general): Здесь продаются книги (Books are sold here). 2) PAST PASSIVE PARTICIPLE (perfective, completed): Книга написана (The book was/has been written). The -ся passive emphasizes the action/process; the participle passive emphasizes the result. Agent is expressed with instrumental case: Книга написана Толстым (written by Tolstoy).",
  "rules": [
    "Reflexive passive (-ся): 3rd person verb + -ся: Книги продаются. (Books are sold.)",
    "Participle passive: short participle: Письмо написано. (The letter has been written.)",
    "Agent = instrumental: Книга написана автором. (The book was written by the author.)",
    "-ся = process/ongoing; participle = result/completed"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Здесь говорится по-русски. (Russian is spoken here., -ся passive), general",
    "Дом был построен в 1990 году. (The house was built in 1990.), participle passive",
    "Эта книга читается легко. (This book reads easily., -ся), characteristic",
    "Работа сделана. (The work is done., short participle), result"
  ],
